menu "Project WiFi Configuration"

    config WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default "431"
        help
            SSID of the WiFi access point this device connects to.
            Set your real SSID via "idf.py menuconfig" or by editing the
            local "sdkconfig" file (that file is git-ignored and NOT
            committed). Keep placeholder values for any committed config.

    config WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi Password"
        default "88888888"
        help
            Password of the WiFi access point.
            Set your real password via "idf.py menuconfig" or by editing
            the local "sdkconfig" file (git-ignored, NOT committed).
            Keep placeholder values for any committed config.

endmenu

menu "Time (SNTP) Configuration"

    config SNTP_SERVER
        string "SNTP/NTP server (hostname or IP)"
        default "pool.ntp.org"
        help
            NTP server used to set the board clock. May be a hostname (resolved
            again on every request, so it also works when the network comes up
            long after boot) or a literal IP address (works even if DNS in the
            LAN is broken).

            The board syncs in the background and retries forever with backoff
            (5 s -> 60 s), so an offline boot is no longer fatal: once the
            network is up the clock is corrected without a reboot. Until a sync
            succeeds the LCD shows "-- (up HH:MM:SS)" instead of a date.

            Set via "idf.py menuconfig" or by editing the local "sdkconfig"
            file (git-ignored, NOT committed). Keep the placeholder value for
            any committed config.

endmenu

menu "Static IP Fallback (subnets where DHCP never answers)"

    config USE_STATIC_IP_FALLBACK
        bool "Fall back to a static IP when DHCP never hands out a lease"
        default n
        help
            On this lab's subnet the DHCP server stopped answering: the board
            associates (L2) but never receives an OFFER, so it has no IP, SNTP
            can never sync and the LCD keeps showing "Time: -- (up HH:MM:SS)"
            with "NTP:--". Neither DHCP-client restarts nor re-association can
            fix that from the firmware side.

            When enabled, wifi_health_check() still gives DHCP its full chance
            (3 client restarts + one forced re-association, ~100 s). If there is
            still no lease it stops the DHCP client, applies the fixed address
            below and marks the board connected - the code path is the same as
            for a normal lease (esp_netif_set_ip_info() posts GOT_IP itself).
            The address stays until reboot; it is re-applied automatically after
            a re-connect because lwIP clears the IP when the link drops.

            Set the four values below in the local sdkconfig (git-ignored) to
            addresses that are free on your subnet, and keep the placeholder
            values in this committed Kconfig default.

    config STATIC_IP_ADDR
        string "Static IPv4 address"
        default "192.168.4.200"
        help
            Address to apply when DHCP does not answer for ~100 s. Must not be
            in use by another host on that segment (nothing may answer its ARP).

    config STATIC_IP_NETMASK
        string "Static IPv4 netmask"
        default "255.255.255.0"

    config STATIC_IP_GATEWAY
        string "Static IPv4 gateway"
        default "192.168.4.1"
        help
            Router of that subnet, so the board can reach the NTP server and the
            PC-side FastAPI receiver.

    config STATIC_IP_DNS
        string "Static DNS server"
        default "223.5.5.5"
        help
            Explicit DNS is required: when DHCP is dead there is no DNS server
            either, so SNTP could not resolve CONFIG_SNTP_SERVER. Ignore this by
            putting a literal IP into CONFIG_SNTP_SERVER instead.

endmenu

menu "Real-Sensor Upload Configuration"

    config SENSOR_DEVICE_ID
        string "Device ID"
        default "esp32s3-eye-0001"
        help
            Unique identifier reported to the server in each upload batch.
            Server stores it as uploads.device_id.

    config SENSOR_SERVER_URL
        string "Server upload URL"
        default "http://10.1.41.14:8000/api/v1/upload"
        help
            Full URL of the FastAPI receiver running on the PC
            (server/main.py). Use the PC's LAN IP (not 127.0.0.1) so the
            board can reach it. Set via "idf.py menuconfig" or by editing
            the local "sdkconfig" file (git-ignored, NOT committed).
            Keep placeholder values for any committed config.

    config SENSOR_TOKEN
        string "Optional upload auth token"
        default ""
        help
            Optional shared secret for POST /api/v1/upload. When non-empty the
            board sends "Authorization: Bearer <token>" and the server
            (started with a matching SENSOR_TOKEN env var) validates it.
            Leave empty for LAN-only debugging (no auth).
            Set your real token via "idf.py menuconfig" or by editing the
            local "sdkconfig" file (git-ignored, NOT committed).
            Keep placeholder values for any committed config.

endmenu
